We looked at the whole project and fixed what we found. The content format is simpler and a specification describes it. Saves are safer. The self-hosted image does more of its own repair work. The editor has a new look.

## Breaking

This release has no migration. Move your content files to the new layout by hand, or start again from your Git history.

**One folder for each entry and each singleton.** An entry is `<collection>/<slug>/index.json`. A singleton is `<name>/index.json`. `media` is a reserved name. `mica migrate-layout` is removed.

**Rich text in a repeater row** is stored in a file named by the key of the row, such as `sections.k3f9a2.body.mdoc`. The row has a `_key` in the JSON. A new order of the rows changes only `index.json`.

**A save keeps what the model does not declare**, the keys and the `.mdoc` files. A `default` fills a field only in a new entry. `withDefaults` is now `withEmptyValues`.

**Stricter model rules.** The model refuses two names that differ only in case, a `slugField` that is not a slug, a lower bound above an upper one, a default that is not a valid value, and a text `pattern` such as `(a+)+`. An unknown field option stops the build.

**A smaller public API for `@micacms/core`.** `getCollection`, `getSingleton`, `uniqueSlug` and `toIssues` are removed. The layout helpers are replaced by `entryFolder` and `entryDataPath`.

**Four published packages:** `@micacms/core`, `@micacms/astro`, `@micacms/editor` and `@micacms/runtime`. `@micacms/editor-ui` and `@micacms/auth-oidc` are no longer published.

**The content root is set in one place:** `defineSite({ root })`. `micaCollections` has no `root` option.

**Self-hosted configuration.**

- `MICA_REPOSITORY_ROOT` is removed. The image finds the content root by its `.mica/schema.json`. Use `MICA_CONTENT_PATH` only when the repository has more than one. The top of the repository cannot be the content root.
- `MICA_PUBLIC_URL` and `MICA_SESSION_SECRET` are always required. `MICA_PUBLIC_URL` is an origin without a path.
- `NODE_ENV` changes nothing. Plain HTTP is allowed only for an address on this machine.
- `MICA_SIGNIN_WINDOW_MS` is now `MICA_SIGNIN_WINDOW_MINUTES`.
- `MICA_ADMIN_ORIGINS` and `MICA_ADMIN_DIR` are for the local editor only.

**`/ready`** has the status `degraded` (still HTTP 200) when something needs a person. It gives one reason for each problem, and `lastSyncAt`. `restart_required` is removed.

**The CLI.** Each command takes only its own options, and a path is always the content root. `mica import` takes `--collection <name>`. `check` and `import` exit with 78 when they find no readable model.

## Added

**A specification of the content format.** Fixtures check it: a test reads each one and writes it back byte for byte.

**A new look for the editor.** It has green actions, a light sidebar, new fonts, status labels with a coloured dot, and a dark mode. Under Appearance, you choose light, dark or the mode of your system.

**One way to change an order.** It works the same for the entries of a collection, the items of a list, the chosen entries of a relation and the files of a media field. Drag the handle, or use the keyboard, or use the arrow buttons.

**A self-hosted image that cares for its clone.**

- It finds its content root in the clone.
- It follows a force push or a new repository URL. It keeps your drafts as conflicts until you choose.
- It starts with the model in its clone, syncs in the background, and holds a new version that it cannot use.
- It runs once for each data volume and finishes work that a stop or a crash interrupted.
- It reads secrets from `MICA_SESSION_SECRET_FILE`, `MICA_OIDC_CLIENT_SECRET_FILE` and `MICA_REPOSITORY_TOKEN_FILE`.
- A `compact` command makes the clone small again, and `check` also tests the identity provider and the data volume.

**The CLI finds the content root** by its `.mica/schema.json` when you give no path.

**A hint in `astro dev`.** A change to `src/mica.ts` logs how to load the new model.

**A recipe, `remove-field.mjs`,** to remove a field from existing content.

## Changed

**Publish, Discard, Delete and Reorder check the revision that the editor saw.** A colleague's later save shows as a conflict. Nothing is lost, and nothing is published unseen.

**Faster at the size we plan for:** 1,000 entries in a collection, 5,000 files and five editors at the same time. Tests check these numbers.

**No whole media file in memory.** An upload streams to disk, and the file route streams back.

**A slow network does not block** the start, the sync or Publish.

**`mica init` writes the model of the starter,** the same one as the getting-started page.

## Fixed

**Security.** The content files refuse a symbolic link out of the content root. A route slug is one folder name. A `media()` value stays inside the content root. A name such as `constructor` is not a collection. Sign-out removes the unsaved form values that the tab kept.

The first Publish of a new project names `git push -u origin HEAD` when the branch has no upstream. `astro add` no longer writes a broken configuration. A missing value reaches your templates empty, never with its default, and templates do not get the `_key` of repeater rows.
